WEBVTT

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.080
<i>A letter?</i>

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.960
<i>It's from the king.</i>

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:55.960
<i>A little bird told me your curse was lifted.</i>

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.930
<i>I am thinking of giving the crown to you.</i>

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.970
<i>Return to Agnapolis at once.</i>

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.560
<i>Why is this happening now?</i>

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.110
What is that, Natsuki?

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.620
They're some Piyo flakes I put together.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.490
They're good.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.620
I should've eaten dinner last night.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.920
I'm starving.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:36.050
Sorry for making you cook breakfast for me.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.590
Let me help you.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.420
It's already done.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.680
Let's eat together.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.600
Did you sleep well, Little Lamb?

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.470
Well...

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:52.150
Actually, an idea for our new song came to me.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.650
What? You were composing?

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.280
Yes.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.990
You're really into composing, aren't you?

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:00.990
Yes.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.860
But I understand.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.120
After listening to that harmony, I was so excited I couldn't sleep.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.540
You were up all night.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.160
So were you, Shou.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.090
I want to sing with Cecil again.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.170
I agree.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:17.880
Yes.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:18.710
Yeah.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.510
Okay, let's eat.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.220
I'll go get Cecil.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.760
Aijima is no longer here.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.730
What?

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.520
This is...

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.780
He returned to Agnapolis to succeed the throne.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.030
He went home?

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.990
To succeed the throne?

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.700
Are you saying Cecil is going to become the king?

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.710
The king of Agnapolis was thinking of stepping down from the throne soon.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.710
That's why he told Aijima to return.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.040
But...

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.100
Cecil was excited to sing with us.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.850
<i>It's a miracle.</i>

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.850
<i>The muses were in that harmony just now.</i>

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.650
Cecil...

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.190
Could this be some kind of mistake?

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.570
That's right!

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:27.120
There's no way he would leave behind the sheet music Haru gave him!

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.700
But he really did go home.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:36.830
Perhaps he left behind the sheet music, so he could forget everything.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.340
But...

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.380
No, it can't be!

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.480
<i>Cecil.</i>

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:06.910
He went back to Agnapolis? That's too bad.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:11.120
I had a feeling something amazing was about to start.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.870
This is ridiculous.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.460
That's why I hate groups.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.250
Trusting them only leads to looking like a fool when you're betrayed.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.210
Ran-Ran, you're too cold!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:28.090
The probability of Cecil returning is practically zero.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.140
<i>I will return!</i>

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.850
<i>Camus, please tell them that!</i>

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.230
<i>Aijima.</i>

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.030
<i>Apparently you cannot change your fate.</i>

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.960
Cecil.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.880
<i>I want to become an idol.</i>

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.180
<i>What?</i>

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:15.970
<i>I want to become an idol and make lots of people happy.</i>

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.730
I can't believe Cecil went home.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.480
It's unthinkable.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.450
I wonder why he left without saying anything.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:41.370
I felt like I had a younger brother after Cecil showed up.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.080
It was fun.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.050
Otoya, me too.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:52.090
<i>Your heart is warm and kind of like a sunny spot.</i>

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:56.060
I loved him since the day we met.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.060
<i>I am not interested in becoming an idol.</i>

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:07.730
<i>I am best suited to singing your songs.</i>

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.280
At first I thought someone ridiculous had showed up, but...

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.250
<i>Why did you become an idol, Masato?</i>

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:23.330
<i>It's Haruka, isn't it? The girl you love.</i>

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.000
Aijima was by our side.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:31.760
Before we knew it, it was natural for him to be there.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.050
<i>Soon, the chains in your heart will disappear.</i>

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.430
<i>You will feel happy from the bottom of your heart.</i>

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.100
He surprised me with his words.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.530
Now that he's gone, it's sad.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.070
<i>It's a miracle.</i>

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:57.700
<i>The muses were in that harmony just now.</i>

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:02.960
<i>Could it be that Cecil's voice goes really well with ours?</i>

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.960
<i>"Spinning seven, I create a constellation."</i>

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.300
<i>This is the will of the muses.</i>

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.720
<i>This is what you wanted to show me...</i>

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:20.560
<i>That I should sing not as one, but as seven.</i>

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:26.730
I do not believe Aijima is one to abandon music so easily.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.770
I agree.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.530
He'll come back, right?

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.740
But if he's succeeding the throne...

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.910
Can it be that easy for him to come back?

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:42.450
Realistically speaking, it's impossible.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.460
So there's no point in waiting for him, then?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.590
This song...

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:29.330
Nanami.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.460
She's composing now?

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.670
A new song for all of us?

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.300
She believes he'll come back.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.560
Nanami.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:51.980
She truly wishes to include Aijima as a member of ST☆RISH.

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:55.110
We must respond.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:56.280
Yes.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.860
To her feelings.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:00.240
Yeah.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.460
<i>What is that?</i>

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.440
It's done.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.620
Amazing.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.700
Lady, you've improved again.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.790
Yes.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.790
This is wonderful, Nanami.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.420
I want to sing right now!

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:59.220
It's like the music is bubbling up from deep inside me!

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.220
You're right...

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:01.930
But we cannot.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:02.590
Huh?

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:06.560
We cannot sing this song unless the seven of us are together.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:10.980
But she wrote this amazing song...

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:14.650
Why don't we write some lyrics together, then?

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.400
That's a good idea.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.820
Once Cecil returns, we can sing it immediately.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.530
Not bad, Natsuki.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:23.700
Everyone.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.290
Let's leave Ceci's parts blank.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.210
Let me show you my songwriting skills!

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.460
They're writing lyrics for a seven-part song, believing he'll return.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:44.970
Fools. Considering the customs of royalty, there is no way he will return.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:47.390
How naïve of them.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:51.890
They'll never last in this world if they keep pretending they're friends.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.110
Shou, what are your lyrics like?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.010
I want to include "with all our might" somewhere.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.150
"With all our might"?

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:02.740
That sounds like something you'd write.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.330
Once we fill in his parts...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.750
The lyrics will be complete.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.080
Yeah.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.300
Hello-bello-bah!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.220
President!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.470
He came so far upstream on a motorboat!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:30.010
Was there no other way to get here?!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:39.150
I bring you some big news today.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:44.030
Your next song has been decided.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.530
Miss Nanami, good work.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:55.500
I have chosen a song from the ones you worked so hard to write.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.580
President, please wait!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.500
I've actually composed a new song!

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:05.590
I finally found what was missing from my new song.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:08.340
What was missing?

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:11.180
Yes. It was Cecil's voice.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.180
Mister Aijima's voice?

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:18.100
If Cecil will sing,

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:20.860
I'm sure it will create

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.940
a wonderful harmony you've never heard before.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:24.610
So, please...

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:28.320
No, no, no!

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:33.290
Mister Aijima has returned to his country.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:35.750
President, you knew.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:40.000
He is already living a different life.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:43.710
You should forget about him immediately.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:47.510
Cecil treasured this pendant.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:50.180
There's no way he would return home without it.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.930
That's right! I know he'll come back!

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.350
President, please give us some more time.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:05.400
Even if Mister Aijima were here, I would not accept it.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.400
Why not?

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.860
Because...

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:14.160
You've been nominated for the Uta☆Pri Award!

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.080
We have?

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.540
The Uta☆Pri Award?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.370
Seriously?

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.330
Serious, serious, seriously!

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:25.960
The hard work and excellent balance of the six

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:30.590
of you have earned you your nomination.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:33.300
But things are just getting started.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.810
Now is a very important time that will determine

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:39.480
whether or not you will win the Uta☆Pri Award, you know.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:43.060
I will never allow you to jeopardize the balance

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:44.610
the six of you have with a dangerous gamble.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.190
Don't be like that!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:46.980
President!

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:53.450
If you request anything else crazy from me, I will decline your nomination.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:56.200
What's gotten into you?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.540
You have to listen to what Shining says.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.920
I will wait for Aijima.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.960
What? Ma!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:04.920
So will I.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:07.960
We want to try singing with him.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.590
We want to sing as seven!

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:11.510
Please!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.720
Ichinose, you too?

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.470
Wh-What happened to all of you?

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:24.400
It seems you do not understand my reasoning.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:30.610
I'm sorry, but for this year's Uta☆Pri Award...

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.410
You'll be spectators.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.580
I'll be in touch!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.540
Please wait!

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.180
Cecil!

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:01.890
Saotome! Are you satisfied with the six-member ST☆RISH?

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.230
If you don't listen to this miraculous harmony,

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.490
you will regret it for the rest of your life!

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.450
Now he's said it.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.120
Cecil.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.730
What are you doing?

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:06.960
This is...

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.210
What's going on?

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.610
What a sound.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:36.110
I want to stay wrapped up in this happy wave forever.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:41.530
<i>I will work hard to produce songs that make those who listen to them happy.</i>

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:46.540
Is this the elusive wave I've been looking for?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.170
The happy pulse?

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.170
Is this the power of seven?

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:54.340
Is this the true form of ST☆RISH?

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:09.150
Boys.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:15.610
Amazing. I had no idea it would create such a wonderful harmony.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.280
Wow.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.700
That was awesome.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:23.080
Aijima.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.200
Ceci.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:31.830
I thought music connected people and the gods.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:39.550
Let's connect with each other

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:38.970
But Haruka's songs also connect people to other people.

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:43.720
I want to bring lots of smiles to everyone's faces.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:47.180
I want to sing with everyone forever.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.020
I will never have another meeting like this.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:53.770
Cecil.

00:18:55.150 --> 00:19:03.820
I was jealous of the bond between everyone else and Haruka, so I...

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.290
<i>I can sing better than anyone else...</i>

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.210
<i>Even better than the members of ST☆</i>RISH!

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:12.120
I...

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:17.210
That's enough. We understand how you feel.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:32.020
We all believed you would return.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:34.810
Cecil.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.770
Let's sing together from now on.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.360
Yes.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:46.700
President, please make me a member of ST☆RISH.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:51.410
President!

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.300
This song and the seven of you...

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:05.340
As the president of Shining Agency, I cannot abandon that here.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:12.310
I shall officially name you again. The seven of you are...

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:18.320
Starting today, you are the new ST☆RISH!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.650
What?!

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:21.940
All right!

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.610
And this song...

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:29.620
As soon as I heard it, it came to me...

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:34.460
The title of this song is <i>Maji LOVE</i>...

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:39.590
My, my, my. You're starting to get the picture.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:42.880
Well, I must go to speak with key government officials

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:46.860
immediately to protect Mister Aijima from...

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:48.800
There is no need for that.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.680
What is that?

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:56.810
This permit from the king allows me to become a member of ST☆RISH.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:58.770
I can't read it.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:02.490
It took some time to get this.

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:12.700
B-B-Bravo!

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.500
Those kids...

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:19.170
He not only refused to succeed the throne, but he got a permit as well.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:23.380
I sent this to Agnapolis out of curiosity.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:30.300
I didn't think he'd complete it so perfectly.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:32.720
You...

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.320
What is that?

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.780
What's happening?

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.440
What an amazing aura.

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:24.940
Yeah.
